<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Garibald I of Bavaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–c. 591</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Garibald I was the first known Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, ruling from about 555 to about 591 as a member of the Agilolfing family under Frankish overlordship. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walderada">Walderada</a>, widow of the Frankish king Theudebald, and his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodelinda">Theodelinda</a> married the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/authari">Authari</a>. His alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a> provoked Frankish intervention, and he was probably deposed around 591.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garibald-i-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="Garibald I of Bavaria" width="320" height="537" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Libro Antiguo se desconoce autor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GARIBALDO_I_DE_BAVIERA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
